# f01 -- READ COMMITTED: the lost update is avoided, not aborted.
#
# Two read committed sessions each set the hot row R1. T2 waits
# for T1's row lock. When T1 commits, T2's write meets a row
# that changed after T2 began: it fails with `updated`, which
# does not abort. T2 reads the newest version with readlatest
# and writes; nothing T1 did is lost.


== pairing RR/RR == T1=RC T2=RC
@1 T1 begin -> ok
@1 T2 begin -> ok
@2 T1 write R1 1 -> ok
@3 T2 write R1 2 blocks -> blocked
@4 T1 commit -> ok
@3 T2 write R1 2 blocks -> updated (resumed)
@5 check last T2 updated -> satisfied
@6 T2 readlatest R1 -> 1
@6 check last T2 1 -> satisfied
@7 T2 write R1 2 -> ok
@8 T2 commit -> ok
@9 check committed T1 T2 -> satisfied
@9 check row R1 2 -> satisfied
